workedExamples.solution_text:
$y'=\frac{1}{x}$
At $P$, the tangent has gradient $1$ and the normal has gradient $-1$.
For the tangent:
$\begin{aligned}y-2&=1(x-1)\\y&=x+1.\end{aligned}$
For the normal:
$\begin{aligned}y-2&=-(x-1)\\y&=-x+3.\end{aligned}$
The sketch shows the point of contact and both lines.
